{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 32, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Arthur woke to the scent of pine needles and damp earth. Sunlight dappled through leaves, illuminating a forest floor carpeted in moss. He stretched, a familiar ache in his back, and blinked. The trees seemed… too perfect. The way the light filtered, the impossibly vibrant green of the foliage – it was hyperreal, almost offensively so. He glanced down at his hands, noticing the texture of the bark embedded in his palms, the slight roughness. A flicker of unease prickled at the back of his neck. He reached out, tentatively touching a nearby tree trunk. The wood felt solid, undeniably real, yet… contained. A small, intricately carved wooden signpost stood nearby, pointing towards a path labeled \"Silverwood Village.\" Arthur frowned, a growing sense of disorientation washing over him. This wasn't his backyard. This wasn't his life.\n\n***\n\nHe began to walk, the path winding deeper into the forest. The air hummed with an almost palpable energy. He noticed details he’d never seen before – tiny, iridescent beetles flitting amongst the flowers, a family of deer grazing peacefully in a clearing. Everything was meticulously crafted, flawlessly rendered. Then he saw it: a shimmering, translucent barrier, subtly outlining a distant, snow-capped mountain. It wasn’t a natural formation; it was a boundary, a code. A wave of nausea hit him, and he stumbled, clutching his head. He looked down at his clothes – a worn flannel shirt and jeans, perfectly unremarkable. But something felt… different. He felt a strange pull, an instinct to *do*. A voice, not his own, whispered in his mind, \"Level up. Explore.\" Arthur realized with chilling certainty: he wasn’t in Kansas anymore. He wasn't even in his own world. He was inside a video game.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.7354406118392944}, {"token": "▁woke", "logprob": -1.7583379745483398}, {"token"